*> Words that are keywords only in some statements: READ PREVIOUS,
*> ROUNDED MODE, ACCEPT FROM DATE YYYYMMDD, screen attributes, CALL
*> STATIC, the GnuCOBOL and IBM special registers. A program that
*> declares an item with such a name (COLOR here) still means the item.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. CONTEXTS.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT KEYED-FILE ASSIGN TO "KEYED"
        ORGANIZATION INDEXED ACCESS DYNAMIC RECORD KEY KEYED-ID.
DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
FD  KEYED-FILE.
01  KEYED-REC.
    05  KEYED-ID        PIC X(4).
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  TODAY               PIC 9(8).
01  AMOUNT              PIC 9(3)V9.
01  RESULT              PIC 9(3).
01  REPLY               PIC X.
01  COLOR               PIC 9 VALUE 2.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    OPEN INPUT KEYED-FILE
    READ KEYED-FILE PREVIOUS
    ACCEPT TODAY FROM DATE YYYYMMDD
    COMPUTE RESULT ROUNDED MODE IS NEAREST-EVEN = AMOUNT
    ACCEPT REPLY WITH AUTO-SKIP REQUIRED
    DISPLAY COLOR UPON STDOUT
    IF COB-CRT-STATUS = 0 AND NUMBER-OF-CALL-PARAMETERS = 0
        CALL STATIC "SUBPROG"
    END-IF
    CLOSE KEYED-FILE
    STOP RUN.
